parts.text:
In button.tsx line 56, I have:
```tsx
style={({ pressed: pressedState }) => [
  styles.button,
  borderStyle,
  { backgroundColor, opacity: disabled || loading ? 0.6 : 1 },
  fullWidth && styles.fullWidth,
  typeof style === 'function' ? style({ pressed: pressedState }) : style,
]}
```

The issue: `style` is typed as `StyleProp<ViewStyle>` which is `ViewStyle | RegisteredStyle<ViewStyle> | RecursiveArray<...> | Falsy | ...`. Calling `style(...)` on it isn't allowed because the union includes non-callables. TypeScript narrowed incorrectly — `typeof style === 'function'` should narrow to the function variant, but `StyleProp<ViewStyle>` doesn't include a function variant (PressableProps style is `StyleProp<ViewStyle> | ((state) => StyleProp<ViewStyle>)`). Since I overrode `style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>`, the function variant is excluded.

Simplest fix: type `style` as `PressableProps['style']` or remove the function call support. Since I destructure and re-pass style, I should just type style as `PressableProps['style']`.

Let me fix: 
```ts
interface ButtonProps extends PressableProps {
  variant?: ButtonVariant;
  loading?: boolean;
  fullWidth?: boolean;
  style?: PressableProps['style'];
  children: React.ReactNode;
}
```

That allows the function form. Let me update.

